PolicyMethodRolesPauseTest
├── when the pause holder pauses an unpaused method
│   ├── it should report paused.
│   └── it should emit Paused with the pause holder.
├── when the pause holder pauses a paused method
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry EnforcedPause.
├── when the pause holder unpauses a paused method
│   ├── it should report not paused.
│   └── it should emit Unpaused with the pause holder.
├── when the pause holder unpauses an unpaused method
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry ExpectedPause.
├── when anyone else pauses
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry OwnableUnauthorizedAccount of the caller.
├── when anyone else unpauses
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry OwnableUnauthorizedAccount of the caller.
├── when the pause holder calls a key admin function
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should leave the keys and the key admin unchanged.
├── when the pause holder renounces while paused
│   ├── it should leave the method paused.
│   └── it should let nobody unpause, the former holder included.
├── when the pause holder renounces while unpaused
│   └── it should let nobody pause.
├── when the pause holder renounces with a transfer open
│   └── it should let no earlier nominee accept.
├── when the pause holder renounces
│   └── it should leave the key admin standing.
├── when the pause holder role is handed over in two steps
│   ├── it should let only the new holder pause.
│   └── it should leave the key admin and the keys unchanged.
├── when the zero address calls after the pause holder renounced while paused
│   ├── it should revert.
│   ├── it should carry OwnableUnauthorizedAccount of the zero address for unpause, pause, transferOwnership and renounceOwnership.
│   └── it should leave the method paused.
└── when the zero address accepts with no transfer open
    ├── it should revert.
    ├── it should carry OwnableUnauthorizedAccount of the zero address.
    └── it should leave the owner unchanged.
